{"name":"Chenille","hex":"#a6cd91","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"chenille","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An extremely soft and bunchy fabric often used to make sweaters."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chenille"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chenille fabric","blocks":[{"text":"Chenille is a type of yarn, or the fabric made from it. Chenille is the French word for caterpillar, whose fur the yarn is supposed to resemble."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Samedyelot.jpg/330px-Samedyelot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chenille_fabric"},{"title":"Acalypha hispida","blocks":[{"text":"Acalypha hispida, the chenille plant, is a flowering shrub which belongs to the family Euphorbiaceae, the subfamily Acalyphinae, and the genus Acalypha. Acalypha is the fourth largest genus of the family Euphorbiaceae, and contains many plants native to Oceania."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Acalypha_Hispida_DS.jpg/330px-Acalypha_Hispida_DS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Acalypha_hispida"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/CINIGLIA_MDT_TL.CM.22.492.jpg/500px-CINIGLIA_MDT_TL.CM.22.492.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/CINIGLIA_MDT_TL.CM.22.492.jpg/1280px-CINIGLIA_MDT_TL.CM.22.492.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/CINIGLIA_MDT_TL.CM.22.492.jpg/500px-CINIGLIA_MDT_TL.CM.22.492.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Chenille fabric","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACINIGLIA_MDT_TL.CM.22.492.jpg"},{"srcset":"https: